            "icon_width": 20,
            "title": "How To Use",
            "content": "<p>Gently remove it from its backing and place it on a clean, hair-free area of your skin. For optimal results, wear the patch for approximately 8 hours.<br/><br/>Avoid stretching the skin prior to application. This helps maintain natural tension and prevents tension blisters, ensuring a smoother application process. Ensure the application area is free from lotions, creams, or oils, as these can interfere with absorption.<br/><br/>Before applying, avoid stretching the skin. This helps maintain natural tension, preventing tension blisters and ensuring a smoother application.<br/><br/>Since every body is different, experiment with different locations to find the area that works best for you, and be sure to rotate patch location on your body with each use.<br/><br/>Wet removal method: Using a wet removal method can reduce the adhesiveness of the product, making it easier to remove. This involves moistening the area before attempting to remove the product.<br/>Using oil for enhanced removal: For optimal results, apply oil to the area before removal.<br/><br/>Oil helps deactivate the adhesive, allowing for an even smoother removal.<br/></p><p></p><p></p><p></p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
